50. Development Plans. __ (1) Subject to the development schemes of the Authority, a Union Council may prepare development plans relating to any matter specified in the First Schedule which may among other details of the plans, include the following :-
(a) nature and location of the scheme or schemes ;
(b) total estimated cost ;
(c) sources of finances ;
(d) date of commencement ;
(e) date of completion ;
(f ) manner of execution ;
(g) agencies responsible for maintenance ;
(h) benefits, tangible or intangible to accrue ; and
(i) such other matters as may be necessary.

(2) The development plan of a Union Council shall be sanctioned in its ordinary meeting.

(3) As far as may be, the schemes included in the development plan shall be included in the budget.

(4) The Federal Government may direct that any specified items of income shall wholly or in part be earmarked for and applied in the implementation of a development plan.

